00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:04.309 align:start position:0%
congratulations your kubernetes  application is in production and the  number of services you own are growing  but as you scale your services in  production you also need to scale your  monitoring  after all you can't fix what you don't  monitor and your monitoring needs to be  as reliable as your application  prometheus is the standard kubernetes  monitoring system which helps you  collect store query and alert on metrics  important to your applications and  infrastructure  as you scale up it can become  challenging to configure and manage  prometheus to keep up with the volume of  metrics from all of your successful  services this can be a thankless task  after all your users don't care about  how you manage your monitoring  infrastructure they care about making  sure they can use your app google cloud  managed service for prometheus is  designed to help you scale your  prometheus-based monitoring  it's fully managed by google removing  operational toil from tasks like  sharding prometheus servers  managing complex scrape configurations  and federating prometheus servers to  make a global data source  by using the same planet scale time  series database that google uses for its  own monitoring  managed service for prometheus enables  users to collect metrics at incredible  scale with zero operational overhead  this puts global monitoring and alerting  within reach enabling you to gather  metrics from all of your services across  the planet  metrics collection within your gke  clusters also becomes easier  as managed service for prometheus  provides managed collectors that you can  run in your various clusters these no  longer need to maintain state in your  own environment as they are built to  write to and store metrics in managed  service for prometheus  all this said  managed service for prometheus is an  in-place replacement for running your  own prometheus servers  which means you can keep using your  existing prometheus alerts and your  existing grafana dashboards managed  service for prometheus supports any  application that uses promql to query  metrics  you can also utilize its integrations  with google cloud monitoring to get  started you'll need to take two steps  first enable managed service for  prometheus in your gke cluster and  deploy prometheus collectors  these can be deployed alongside your  existing prometheus servers  these collectors will be configured to  write metrics directly to manage service  for prometheus  second connect clients such as grafana  or other tools you may use to read  prometheus metrics from managed service  for prometheus  and that's it with managed service for  prometheus now you're ready to spend  less time configuring monitoring  infrastructure and more time adding the  next big feature to your app  want to learn more  check out more details in the links  below  [Music]
 

